# EBS QA Rules

Do not consider meaningful work complete until verification is performed.

For normal code changes, prefer:

npm run verify

That command runs lint, TypeScript typecheck, and the production build. If a relevant test suite exists, include it in `verify` before the production build.

If `npm run verify` fails, report which stage failed (lint, typecheck, tests, or build) and the root cause. Do not weaken linting, disable TypeScript checks, or change application code only to force the command to pass.

Run the project test suite when relevant and it is not already covered by `npm run verify`.

For UI work, manually verify:

- desktop
- tablet
- 375px mobile
- no horizontal overflow
- keyboard navigation
- visible focus states
- reduced motion
- CTA behavior
- responsive layout
- browser Back when relevant

For form/workflow changes, verify:

- valid input
- invalid input
- loading state
- error state
- success state
- route transitions

For production-facing changes, verify:

- no debug copy
- no placeholder text
- no broken links
- no fake data
- no stale product statuses

Do not change tests merely to make a failing implementation pass unless the product behavior intentionally changed.

If a test must change, explain why.

When reporting completion, include:

- files changed
- functionality changed
- functionality intentionally preserved
- test/build results
- known limitations
- recommended next step
